.TH CRSF-VIZ 1 "2026-10-29" "crsf-viz 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
crsf\-viz \- visualize CRSF RC channels in a terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crsf\-viz
.RB [ \-\-udp
.IR HOST:PORT
.RB | \-\-serial
.IR DEV
.RB | \-\-unix\-dgram
.IR PATH
.RB | \-\-unix\-stream
.IR PATH
.RB | \-\-stdin ]
.RB [ \-\-baud
.IR BAUD ]
.br
.B crsf\-viz
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B crsf\-viz
displays live CRSF radio-control channels as two stick boxes, numeric
pulse widths, and twelve AUX bars with LOW, MID, or HIGH switch positions.
It runs in a Linux terminal and reads raw CRSF bytes from one selected source.
With no source option, it listens for UDP on
.BR 0.0.0.0:5555 .
.PP
Only valid
.B RC_CHANNELS_PACKED
frames (type
.BR 0x16 )
update the display. CRC8 DVB-S2 is checked before the sixteen packed channels
are decoded. Other CRSF frame types are ignored.
.PP
The display uses the Mode 2 mapping:
.RS
.nf
CH1         Roll       Right stick, horizontal
CH2         Pitch      Right stick, vertical
CH3         Throttle   Left stick, vertical
CH4         Yaw        Left stick, horizontal
CH5-CH16    AUX1-AUX12 Channel bar and switch position
.fi
.RE
.PP
The status line shows the number of accepted RC frames, their incoming rate
as
.BR fps ,
and the link state. The screen refresh is limited to 30 Hz;
.B fps
is the packet rate rather than the screen refresh rate.
After 0.5 seconds without a valid RC frame, the link state becomes
.BR "NO SIGNAL" .
The last channel values remain visible until new frames arrive.
.PP
A terminal at least 80 columns wide and 33 rows high shows the full interface.
Smaller terminals show a resize prompt while input processing continues.
.SH OPTIONS
The source options are mutually exclusive.
.TP
.BI \-\-udp " HOST:PORT"
Bind a UDP socket to the specified local address and port. The default is
.BR 0.0.0.0:5555 ,
which listens on all local IPv4 interfaces. Use
.B 127.0.0.1:5555
to accept only local traffic. The host must be nonempty and the port must
be in the range 1 through 65535. The sender must supply raw CRSF bytes,
not JSON or text.
.TP
.BI \-\-serial " DEV"
Read CRSF bytes directly from a serial device, for example
.BR /dev/ttyUSB0 .
This mode requires the optional
.B pyserial
dependency and permission to open the device.
.TP
.BI \-\-baud " BAUD"
Set the serial baud rate to a positive integer. The default is
.BR 420000 .
This option is used by
.BR \-\-serial .
.TP
.BI \-\-unix\-dgram " PATH"
Create and bind an AF_UNIX datagram socket at
.IR PATH .
A local forwarder sends raw CRSF datagrams to this path.
The path must not already exist. The socket path is removed when the
application closes normally. Remove a confirmed stale socket yourself
or choose another path before restarting.
.TP
.BI \-\-unix\-stream " PATH"
Connect as a client to an existing AF_UNIX stream server at
.IR PATH .
The server must already be listening and must send raw CRSF bytes.
The visualizer does not create or remove this server's socket path.
.TP
.B \-\-stdin
Read raw CRSF bytes from standard input. A controlling terminal is required:
keyboard input and curses output use
.B /dev/tty
so they do not consume or overwrite the incoming byte stream.
This mode can be used in a Bash
.BR tee (1)
pipeline.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Show command-line help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the program name and version, then exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR q , " Q", " Esc"
Quit normally.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Interrupt the program and restore the terminal.
.SH EXAMPLES
Inspect CRSF sent to a local UDP port:
.PP
.RS
.nf
crsf-viz --udp 127.0.0.1:5555
.fi
.RE
.PP
Read a receiver through a USB-UART adapter:
.PP
.RS
.nf
crsf-viz --serial /dev/ttyUSB0 --baud 420000
.fi
.RE
.PP
Listen for a local datagram forwarder:
.PP
.RS
.nf
crsf-viz --unix-dgram /tmp/crsf.sock
.fi
.RE
.PP
Attach to an already running UNIX stream server:
.PP
.RS
.nf
crsf-viz --unix-stream /tmp/crsf.sock
.fi
.RE
.PP
Read a file containing raw CRSF frames while using the controlling terminal
for the interface:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cat frames.crsf | crsf-viz --stdin
.fi
.RE
.PP
Observe a copy of a byte stream in Bash:
.PP
.RS
.nf
producer | tee >(crsf-viz --stdin) | main_consumer
.fi
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERM
Terminal type used by curses. It must identify a terminal with a matching
terminfo entry.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal quit or end of input.
.TP
.B 1
Operational error, such as an unavailable socket, serial device, terminal,
or optional dependency.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line arguments.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted with Ctrl+C.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /dev/tty
Controlling terminal used by
.BR \-\-stdin .
.TP
.B /dev/ttyUSB0
Example Linux USB serial device; specify the actual device with
.BR \-\-serial .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR python3 (1),
.BR socat (1),
.BR tee (1)
.PP
Project and issue tracker:
.UR https://github.com/kewl-ua/crsf_ascii_visualizer
.UE
